  "result": "The fix is planned but not applied. Plan mode is still active and the exit tool is disabled in this session, so I haven't edited any source files.\n\n**Cause:** in `src/click/core.py:386-394`, `Context.__init__` gives a child context the parent's whole `default_map` (`default_map = parent.default_map`). It should give it only the sub-dict for that subcommand (`parent.default_map.get(info_name)`). As written, a nested map like `{\"sub\": {\"opt\": \"x\"}}` is never found, because `opt` is looked up at the top level.\n\n**Plan** (saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-moonlit-kahn.md`):\n1. Change that line to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. It returns `None` when there is no entry for the subcommand, which `lookup_default` already handles.\n2. Add a regression test for a group with `default_map={\"sub\": {\"opt\": \"x\"}}`, including a nested-group case.\n3. Add a changelog entry in `CHANGES.rst`.\n4. Run `pytest`.\n\nIf you approve, or exit plan mode, I'll apply it.",
